35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wow, I found some really important things! The bin house at the station block smells super sour in the summer because you can't wash the floor! We definitely shouldn't do that, or it'll be yucky!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"That sounds unpleasant, Rin. Thank you for warning us. I found that we're spending about 34,000 yen annually on maintenance, and new shelters can be quite expensive, even with the ward's 40% subsidy.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems the ""burden"" Asuka mentioned is quite literal. Most complaints come from the household right next to the bins. It's no wonder the atmosphere is tense; one person is doing all the suffering.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, that's exactly what I was afraid of. It's always one person who ends up doing everything. Also, the truck arrives as early as 7:40, which means the timing is incredibly tight for whoever is managing it.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, your findings confirm my concerns. My measurements show that the frontages vary significantly; some cannot even accommodate a bay. We cannot simply maintain the status quo or choose a design that ignores these physical disparities.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@May, 7:40 is so early! I'd still be sleepy! But if we do the ""supervised mornings"" like the next lane, it's only 20 times a year. That doesn't sound too bad, right? It's like a little morning adventure!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, that sounds like a lovely way to look at it! However, if we add a new system, I worry about the cost. With maintenance already at 34,000 yen, we must be careful not to overspend.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, calling it an ""adventure"" is a stretch. If we force people to police each other's trash at 7:40 AM, we're just creating new opportunities for them to argue. We need a solution that reduces friction, not adds to it.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Rin, ""adventure"" is a cute word for it, but @Shunichi is right. If the system is too rigid or demanding, the person who's ""too sleepy"" just becomes the person everyone else complains about. We need a low-maintenance plan.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, a rotating schedule is a start, but it doesn't address the physical burden. My research into the station block shows that even with a structure, disputes over maintenance and cleaning persist. We need a plan that addresses both labor and location.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we don't have a bin house, we can just wash the ground! @Asuka, if we move the spot or share the work, will it stop being so unfair for the person living right next to it?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I hope so, Rin. If we can share the effort and the cost, it would be much kinder. I'm just worried that a big change might be too expensive for some of us to handle.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, cost is a secondary issue compared to the social cost of this feud. If we just save a few yen but keep the current location, we're essentially paying for a permanent grudge. We need a shift in location or responsibility.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you're on a roll with the drama! But seriously, if we move it, we have to consider the paperwork. The ward requires a site plan and five signatures for a permanent build, which sounds like a total headache to organize.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@May, the paperwork is a necessary hurdle for a permanent solution. If we avoid the effort of filing, we are simply choosing to let one neighbor continue to bear the burden. We must prioritize fairness over convenience.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I don't want anyone to be grumpy! If we move the spot and take turns watching it, everyone can be happy and the air will smell fresh! Let's pick the one that's the most fair!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree, Rin. Let's find a balance where the cost is manageable and the effort is shared. I'll support whatever option ensures no one is unfairly burdened, whether financially or physically.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's be realistic: ""everyone being happy"" is a fantasy. What we need is a compromise that stops the bleeding. If we move the point or rotate the burden, we might actually be able to speak to each other again.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Asuka, you're so intense! But I get it. Let's just make sure that whatever ""fair"" system we pick doesn't turn into a nightmare of endless chores and paperwork for just one of us. I'm ready to vote!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I am not being intense; I am being precise. We have the data: the frontages are unequal and the current location is a source of resentment. I will vote for the option that ensures a genuine redistribution of the burden.,"{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
